---
title: Pumpkin Cheesecake
servings: 8
image: https://joyfoodsunshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/pumpkin-cheesecake-recipe-11.jpg
---

== Crust ==

Mix @graham crackers{2%cups}(crushed, approximately 1.6 wax packages), @sugar{1/2%cup}, and @butter{1/2%cup}(melted) in a #food processor{}.

Press the graham cracker mixture into a #9" pie pan{} until a crust forms. Set aside.

== Filling ==

Blend @cream cheese{2%8oz packages}(), @eggs{2}, @sugar{2/3%cup}, @vanilla{1%tsp}, and @?pumpkin spice{}(to taste) together until smooth.

Add @pure pumpkin{}(get a standard can size, but know you won't use all of it) a few dollops at a time until the mixture is a light/creamy pumpkin color and taste.

> Making a small batch of pumpkin muffins is a great way to use up the remainder of the can.

Pour the filling into the pie crust and spread until even. Bake at 375*F for ~{20%minutes}.

Let stand for ~{15%minutes}.

== Topping ==

Combine @sour cream{1%cup}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @vanilla{1%tsp}, and @?pumpkin spice{}(to taste).

Evenly spread the topping on, optionally sprinkling some leftover crumb mixture on top if you still have it.

Return the cheesecake to a 425*F oven for ~{10%minutes}.

Let cool and chill before serving.